<!DOCTYPE airframe SYSTEM "../airframe.dtd">
<airframe name="Tempest">
  <description>
    Glider fixedwing airframe to test forever soaring and energy control

    + Model:       VolantexRC Ranger 2400 757-9
    + Autopilot:   PX4FMU 5.0 in the form of a Pixhawk 4
    + Actuators:   Serial bus fast MG 12g servos
    + GNSS         2x ublox ZED F9P GNSS
    + MAG          One external RM3100, also a HMC on both GNSS devices
    + ESC:         AM32 70A
    + RCRX:        OpenRXSR Receiver
    + AIRSPEED:    DSP3x
    + TELEMETRY:   Si10xx SiK based tranceiver
    + CURRENT:     3DR branded powerbrick
    + RANGEFINDER: TFMini S on I2C
    + MOTOR:       RPM/V Outrunner Brushless 
    + PROP:        2 blade APC thin electric 10x6"
    + BAT:         18650 Samsung Li-Ion 4S 5000mAh 25C 45CBurst

    NOTES:
    + INDI controled satabilization
    + Using Enahanced Total Energy control with soaring extention
    + FC arrow point to front of airframe
    + Engine battery voltage and current values via separate sensor
    + Servos powered via specific BEC
    + Flightcontroller powered via Powerbrick
    + Telemetry powerd via BEC on powerbrick
    + Si10xx Chip based with firmware enabling PPRZ RSSI message
    + Uploading of the firmware can be performed via original PX4 bootloader, SWD or DFU
      Simple, USB cable in, upload... voila PPRZ aircraft on your Flightcontroller
    + A GNSS device with ANOTHER magneto on it is used, externally...
    + On RSSI in we have an aditional sensor

    + GNSS set to ~19Hz update rate, 4 constelations, RTK onboard setup for heading via GNSS
    + Advised battery for this airframe is a 5000mAh 4S LiPo min. 10C
    ++ Alternatively a 4S LiPo 6500mAh battery pack can be used

    + If testing "Classic" (as in not ETECS..) make sure to disable the settings/estimation/ac_char
    + Set the USE_AIRSPEED value to FALSE at first, for no airspeed tests
    + Use flightplan_forever_soaring.xml for testing
  </description>

